==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|coldliche}}, {{m|enm|caldeliche}}, perhaps borrowed from {{der|en|non|kaldliga|t=coldly}}; equivalent to {{suf|en|cold|ly|id2=adverbial}}. Displaced {{cog|enm|colde|t=coldly}}, from {{cog|ang|cealde|t=coldly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈkəʊldli/}}
* {{a|GA}} {{enPR|kōldʹlē}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈkoʊldli/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-coldly.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{hyph|en|cold|ly}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# in a [[cold]] or [[uncaring]] manner; [[indifferently]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1891|author=w:Thomas Hardy|title=w:Tess of the d'Urbervilles|publisher=James R. Osgood, McIlvaine and Co.|location=London|volume=1|page=82|passage='He is a mighty handsome man!' 'I don't think so,' said Tess '''coldly'''.}}

